{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Belaṭṭhasīsa","html":"<article id='thag1.16'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.16 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.16 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dutiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Two </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Belaṭṭhasīsattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Belaṭṭhasīsa </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yathāpi bhaddo ājañño, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Just as a fine thoroughbred </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>naṅgalāvattanī sikhī; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>proceeds with ease, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Gacchati appakasirena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>tail and mane flying in the wind; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>evaṁ rattindivā mama; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>so my days and nights </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Gacchanti appakasirena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>proceed with ease, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sukhe laddhe nirāmise”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>full of joy not of the flesh. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Belaṭṭhasīso thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
